        "severity": "major",
        "evidence": "down-quark-properties.md:2-3 'The up and down quarks are the same knot type (unknot) in the same environment (Borromean-linked in a color tube).'",
        "notes": "If up and down are literally the same unknot in the same Borromean environment, the only distinguisher is crossing orientation (md:6-8). But an unknot has no intrinsic crossing sign, and orientation reversal of one Borromean component does not by itself change knot/link type — so 'same knot type, differ only in crossing orientation' is in tension with the sibling down-quark.md:14-17 claiming the reversal yields a distinct Skein/charge contribution (-1/3). The mass-splitting mechanism rests on an orientation DOF whose well-definedness for an unknot is asserted, not shown. Marked warn (not fail) because it is an interpretive remark over the conjectural Borromean-quark picture, not a theorem."
      }
