        "notes": "verdict: major-revision. referee_argument: The remark's mass-splitting mechanism rests on a crossing-orientation degree of freedom (da-hidden-dof) that distinguishes two otherwise-identical unknots, with a causal 'so ... different Skein resolution energy' (da-non-sequitur) whose energy-mapping lemma is not supplied and whose key term 'Skein resolution energy' is undefined in-block (da-definitional-ambiguity). The strongest single objection is physical (da-physical-implausibility): identifying the up and down quarks as the same unknot/neutrino differing only by crossing orientation contradicts their status as distinct fermions with charges +2/3 and -1/3. Acceptable only as an explicitly-conjectural interpretation under conj:borromean-quark; should soften 'arises from' to 'is conjectured to arise from' and define the resolution-energy quantity it invokes."
